1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,400
A few people asked me what you're actually meant to do with Scout when your team's on defense or getting completely rolled or you're playing on some narrow map like Dust Bowl where there's barely anywhere to move.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,200
And they all sound like different questions, but it's pretty much the same problem.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:15,400
You can't just hold W and take whatever fight you want anymore.

4
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,600
Because Scout feels ridiculous when your team's doing well.

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:25,400
Everyone's distracted, people are getting separated, you've got space to run around and you're usually the first person there whenever a fight opens up.

6
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:29,720
But the second your team loses all that pressure and every doorway starts getting watched,

7
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:32,440
Scout can go from feeling like he has no limitations,

8
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,000
to feeling like one of the most useless classes in the game.

9
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:42,760
So a lot of this video is going to be about slowing down a bit, using chip damage,

10
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:45,800
sitting further back on high ground where you can actually see what's going on,

11
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:49,560
and waiting for someone to overextend instead of launching yourself into three people every

12
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:53,480
time you see their backs turned. Because even when an opening looks really good,

13
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:57,400
You still have to think about whether your team is alive, whether anyone can actually help you,

14
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:01,240
and whether dying for that play is even worth it, especially when you're defending on red

15
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:05,640
in payload or attack defend, because you can't take your life for granted like Blue Team Cat,

16
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:12,120
because those respawn times on certain maps get just ridiculous, and one bad death can take you

17
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:16,920
out of the fight for what feels like forever. And Scout can create way more for his team than

18
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:21,400
the scoreboard actually shows. You can make half the enemy team turn around, pull someone away from

19
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,400
2.

20
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:24,640
You can either stay away from the objective or force their medic backwards, but your team

21
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:27,580
