54
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:52,060
Like the last clip, this is a defensive situation that isn't as straightforward as holding a boxed in last with two obvious flanks.

55
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:55,520
When you're forced to fight in more open areas without much pressure from your team,

56
00:03:55,520 --> 00:04:00,160
Scout needs to take some of that pressure off them by becoming the center of attention without just throwing his life away.

57
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:08,080
It's about occupying spaces the enemy can't ignore, forcing them to deal with you and drawing attention away from your team while still prioritizing survivability.

58
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:21,1000
Once your team is no longer occupying the space you were trying to defend and the enemy has taken full control of that area,

59
00:04:21,1000 --> 00:04:26,720
your presence there becomes much less valuable. If you still have space behind you to retreat into,

60
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:31,120
use it. There's no reason to keep testing an area your team no longer has any presence in,

61
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:35,040
especially when you're on defence. Your job isn't to take the space back by yourself,

62
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:39,280
it's to stay alive, continue slowing them down, and keep running time off the clock.

63
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:42,560
But you need to be alive to do this. Where blue team is all about trying to

64
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:46,800
get one big coordinated push to break through, red is more about survivability.

